{
  // The write door's type check, and the reminder job's.
  //
  // It is separate from _shared/muse/tsconfig.json only because that config's
  // `include` is relative to its own folder. The settings are the same ones, kept
  // in one place and extended here, so the two doors cannot end up compiled under
  // different rules — which is the same reason they now share one az.ts and one
  // scrub.ts instead of carrying a copy each.
  //
  // WHY IT MATTERS MORE HERE THAN ANYWHERE ELSE IN THIS REPO. Nothing under
  // supabase/functions was type-checked before the doors: tsconfig.app.json ends
  // with `"include": ["src"]`. On a read door an uncaught type slip is a wrong
  // number in a chat; on a write door it is a wrong row in the ledger, written
  // without anybody looking at a screen.
  //
  // index.ts and dbSupabase.ts are deliberately left out of both configs: they
  // import `jsr:@supabase/…` and use Deno globals, which plain tsc cannot resolve.
  // That is exactly why they hold the runtime wiring and no decisions — everything
  // that decides anything is in the files below, and tests/museWrite.test.ts runs
  // those for real.
  "extends": "../_shared/muse/tsconfig.json",
  // dbFinanceSupabase.ts joins index.ts and dbSupabase.ts on the excluded list, for
  // the same reason: it is the other half of the Supabase wiring and holds no
  // decisions. The interfaces and the tool files are checked, and they are where every
  // decision is.
  // dbFinanceSupabase.ts and dbMemory.ts join index.ts and dbSupabase.ts on the excluded
  // list, for the same reason: they are the other halves of the Supabase wiring and hold
  // no decisions. Everything else is in here, one file per line so adding the next one is
  // a one-line diff rather than a re-wrap.
  "include": [
    "db.ts",
    "dbFinance.ts",
    "gated.ts",
    "handler.ts",
    "healthTools.ts",
    "kit.ts",
    "memoryDb.ts",
    "memoryWrites.ts",
    "openapi.ts",
    "tools.ts",
    "toolsFinance.ts",
    "undoContract.ts",
    "undoRegistry.ts",
    "../cron-reminders/schedule.ts"
  ]
}
